              "description": "OPEN vocabulary — how the build OBTAINS this dependency. Recommended values: system (find_package/expected pre-installed), vendored (source copied into the tree), fetchcontent (CMake FetchContent), download_build (ExternalProject/custom download-source-and-build), submodule (git submodule), package_manager (vcpkg/conan/pip/npm/maven), prebuilt_binary (binary shipped in repo). If none fits, coin a concise lowercase token (e.g. conda, apt, cpm, git_subtree, runtime_download) AND record it in meta.observations. Also set the closed `locality` field accordingly."},
            "locality": {"type": "string",
              "enum": ["local", "remote", "system", "runtime", "unknown"],
              "description": "STABLE axis (model-set): local=already in repo (vendored/prebuilt); remote=pulled from outside (fetchcontent/download/submodule/registry); system=expected pre-installed via find_package; runtime=loaded at runtime; unknown"},
            "source": {"type": "string", "description": "model: WHERE it is obtained from — download URL / registry / 'system (find_package, must be pre-installed)' / in-tree path, 简体中文"},
            "declared_in": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"},
              "description": "model: repo file(s) that declare how this dependency is integrated, e.g. the CMakeLists.txt with find_package/FetchContent_Declare/ExternalProject_Add/target_link_libraries, a .gitmodules entry, or a requirements/manifest line"},
            "used_symbols": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"},
              "description": "model (best-effort, codegraph/grep): the dependency's public symbols / APIs THIS library actually calls (e.g. cairo_create, BIO_new, numpy.ndarray). Consumed by dim-9 bottom-up rollup: a child's un-adaptable API only blocks this (parent) library if it appears here. Omit/empty for system deps or when usage can't be pinned down (rollup then falls back to dependency scope)."},
